# CONCERNING

# THE IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN

# BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

# THE REGENT OF HULU SUNGAI UTARA,

Considering:  
a. that in the context of protecting the rights of women and children as mandated by the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia, improving the quality of life of women and children and addressing all forms of violence against women and children, there needs to be concern from all parties, both the community and related government institutions and law enforcement officials;  
b. that there is a tendency of increasing victims and cases of violence against women and children, which have not been handled optimally so that integrated services are needed by relevant agencies and community institutions/organizations to provide protection for women and children victims of violence;  
c. that in an effort to facilitate women and children to improve their skills and independence and to obtain consultation services and problem solving experienced by women and children, a center for integrated services for the empowerment of women and children is needed;  
d. that based on the considerations referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Protection of Women and Children;  

In View of:  
1. Law Number 27 of 1959 concerning the Stipulation of Law Number 3 Drt. of 1953 concerning the Establishment of Level II Regions in Kalimantan (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1953 Number 9, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 2756), as Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1959 Number 72, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1820);  

2. Law Number 4 of 1979 concerning Child Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1979 Number 32, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3143);  
3. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (Convention on The Elimination off all Forms of Discrimination Against Women) (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3277);  
4. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);  
5. Law Number 26 of 2000 concerning Human Rights Courts (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2000 Number 208, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4026);  
6. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235), as amended by Law Number 35 of 2014 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 297, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5606);  
7. Law Number 13 of 2003 concerning Manpower (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2003 Number 39, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4279);  
8. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);  
9. Law Number 33 of 2004 concerning Financial Balance Between the Central Government and Regional Governments (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 No. 126, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4438);  
10. Law Number 39 of 2004 concerning the Placement and Protection of Indonesian Migrant Workers Abroad;  

11. Law Number 11 of 2005 concerning Ratification of the International Covenant on Economic, Social and Cultural Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2005 Number 118, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4557);  
12. Law Number 12 of 2005 concerning Ratification of the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2005 Number 119, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4558);  
13. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (PTPPO) (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);  
14. Law Number 12 of 2011 concerning the Formulation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5234);  
15. Law Number 11 of 2012 concerning the Juvenile Criminal Justice System (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2012 Number 153, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5332);  
16. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587, as has been amended several times most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);  
17. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning the Implementation and Cooperation for the Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4644);  
18. Government Regulation Number 9 of 2008 concerning Procedures and Mechanisms for Integrated Services for Witnesses and/or Victims of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2008 Number 22, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4818);  
19. Presidential Regulation Number 87 of 2014 concerning Implementing Regulations of Law Number 12 of 2011 Concerning the Formulation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 199);  
20. Presidential Decree Number 36 of 1999 concerning Ratification of the Convention On The Right Of The Child (Convention on the Rights of the Child);  
21. Presidential Decree Number 59 of 2002 concerning the National Action Plan for the Elimination of the Worst Forms of Child Labor;  
22. Presidential Decree Number 87 of 2002 concerning the National Action Plan for the Elimination of Commercial Exploitation of Children;  
23. Regulation of the Chief of the National Police Number 3 of 2008 concerning the Establishment of Special Service Rooms and Procedures for Examination of Witnesses and /Or Victims of Criminal Acts;  
24. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 80 of 2015 concerning the Formulation of Regional Legal Products (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 2036);  
25. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2008 concerning the Implementation of Women's Protection;  
26. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 3 of 2008 concerning the Implementation of Child Protection;  
27. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 1 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards (SPM) for Integrated Services for Women and Children Victims of Violence;  
