#### Article 16

1. To prevent acts of violence against women and children, the Regional Government shall carry out empowerment and awareness raising to families, parents, and the community by providing information, guidance and/or counseling.  
2. In addition to empowerment and awareness raising as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government shall undertake efforts as follows:
   a. increasing the quantity and quality of education both formal and non-formal and informal;  
   b. opening accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income enhancement and social services;  
   c. opening employment opportunities for women;  
   d. building community participation and concern to implement prevention and protection of women and children from acts of violence;  
   e. building and providing a complete and easily accessible information system;  
   f. imposing curfew restrictions for children (under 18 years) going out at night no later than 11.00 pm, if beyond that time must be accompanied by parents or family;  
   g. restricting children's access to the internet at internet cafes (warnet) during school hours;  
   h. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care for women and children; and  
   i. opening complaint posts for the protection of women and children from acts of violence.

#### Article 17

1. Prevention of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 16, shall be implemented by SKPD whose duties and functions are in the fields of: Perda Kab. HSU Tahun 2016 Nomor 3 ttg Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak / Regional Regulation of HSU Regency Year 2016 Number 3 concerning Protection of Women and Children:
   a. social affairs;  
   b. health;  
   c. education;  
   d. manpower;  
   e. women's empowerment and child protection;  
   f. mental and spiritual; and  
   g. peace and order.  
2. Prevention of acts of violence by SKPD as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in an integrated and sustainable manner based on the Regional Action Plan.

## Part Four

Assistance Mechanism

#### Article 18

1. Assistance shall be implemented by persons and/or institutions that cooperate with P2TP2A and PIK Keluarga.  
2. The assistance mechanism as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be organized according to standard operating procedures that are further regulated by a Regent Regulation.

## Part Five

Principles of Service and Assistance

#### Article 19

The provision of services and assistance to victims shall be carried out with the principles of:

a. fast, safe, and empathetic;  
b. guarantee of confidentiality;  
c. easily accessible; and  
d. free of charge.

## Part Six

Services for Victims of Acts of Violence

#### Article 20

1. Forms of services provided to women and children victims of acts of violence, are as follows:
   a. complaint services;  
   b. health services;  
   c. legal aid;  
   d. repatriation;  
   e. rehabilitation, social reintegration, and medicolegal;  
   f. identification services; and  
   g. psychological services.  
2. Forms of services as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in accordance with minimum service standards established by the Government and implemented by SKPD whose duties and functions are in the fields of: Perda Kab. HSU Tahun 2016 Nomor 3 ttg Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak / Regional Regulation of HSU Regency Year 2016 Number 3 concerning Protection of Women and Children:
   a. social affairs;  
   b. health;  
   c. women's empowerment and child protection; and  
   d. mental and spiritual.  
3. In carrying out the duties and functions as referred to in paragraph (2), the Regional Government shall cooperate with Government agencies, Provincial Government, other Regency/City Governments, and the community.  
4. Further provisions regarding procedures for services and handling of women and children victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), paragraph (2), and paragraph (3), shall be regulated by a Regent Regulation.

#### Article 21

1. The Regional Government is obligated to provide complaint services and provision of special service rooms at police stations, in order to provide protection to women and children from acts of violence.  
2. The Regional Government and the community or social service institutions may establish recovery houses or safe houses.  
3. Further provisions regarding complaint services and social services as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2), shall be regulated by a Regent Regulation.

## Part Seven

Empowerment of Victims of Acts of Violence

#### Article 22

1. The Regional Government is obligated to carry out empowerment of women victims of acts of violence.  
2. Empowerment of victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented by P2TP2A.  
3. In carrying out empowerment of women victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government shall prepare empowerment programs in the economic field, which include:
   a. providing the necessary requirements for entrepreneurship training for women, in order to increase business knowledge, attitudes, and skills;  
   b. facilitating the implementation of various job training and skills training;  
   c. providing assistance in developing productive economic enterprises;  
   d. exploring cooperation with small, medium and large enterprises, as well as financial institutions to develop women's businesses;  
   e. endeavoring to provide capital for women victims of acts of violence; and  
   f. expanding access to information and promoting women's products.  
4. In carrying out empowerment of women victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government may establish cooperation with job training institutions organized by the private sector.

#### Article 23

1. Empowerment of women victims of acts of violence as referred to in Article 22, shall be carried out by providing training to increase capability, skills, and independence.  
2. Training as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be carried out through:
   a. on the job training;  
   b. pre employment training; and  
   c. understudy training.

# CHAPTER VII

## COOPERATION AND PARTNERSHIP

## Part One

Cooperation

#### Article 24

1. In order to achieve the objectives of providing protection to women and children from acts of violence as referred to in Article 3, the Regional Government shall cooperate with:
   a. the government;  
   b. the provincial government;  
   c. other regency/city governments;  
   d. universities; and  
   e. non-governmental institutions.  
2. Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1), shall include:
   a. exchange of data and information;  
   b. rehabilitation of victims of acts of violence;  
   c. repatriation and social reintegration; and  
   d. provision of evidence and witnesses, and followed up in accordance with applicable law.  
3. Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2), shall be set forth in the form of a joint agreement.

## Part Two

Partnership

#### Article 25

1. The Regional Government shall establish partnerships with the business world in the provision of protection to women and children from acts of violence.  

Perda Kab. HSU Tahun 2016 Nomor 3 ttg Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak / Regional Regulation of HSU Regency Year 2016 Number 3 concerning Protection of Women and Children

2. Partnership as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be carried out through:
   a. notification of information on employment opportunities for women victims of acts of violence;  
   b. education and training for women victims of acts of violence;  
   c. educational assistance for women and children victims of acts of violence whose education has been interrupted; and  
   d. fostering and increasing the economic independence of women victims of acts of violence.  
3. Partnership as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2), shall be set forth in the form of an agreement.
